                "element_id": 1,
                "text": "The Structure of an HTML File",
                "category": "title_candidate",
                "reason": "First text element of the slide"
            },
            {
                "element_id": 2,
                "text": "An HTML file consists of the text to be displayed on the page, interspersed with various directives enclosed in angle brackets, which are known as tags.\nHTML tags generally occur in pairs. The opening tag begins with the tag name. The corresponding closing tag has the same name preceded by a slash. The effect of the tag applies to everything between the opening and closing tags.\nThe only HTML tags you will need before Week 7 of the course course appear in the template on the next page, which describes the structure of the HTML index file (and by convention is called index.html.)",
                "category": "paragraph_candidate",
                "reason": "Multiple complete explanatory sentences detected"
            }
        ]
    },
